  "documentation": {
    "range": "This species is native to South America, and has been introduced to North America, Europe, Africa, and Asia (not all these introduced locations are mapped here) (Bertolino 2005). It is patchily distributed throughout its historic range in association with mesic habitats and water bodies. Its distribution in the Patagonian steppe is likely the result of human introduction (Ojeda, Lessa, and Bidau pers. comm.).",
    "population": "It is increasing in number, and is considered a pest in parts of its range and has been the subject of eradication measures (Bertolino 2005).",
    "habitats": "This species prefers habitats near water, and is rarely observed more than 100 m away from rivers (Bertolino 2005).",
    "threats": "There are no major threats to this species (Bertolino 2005). In parts of Argentina, however, it is considered endangered. Cattle ranchers have eliminated it from much of the centre of its native range.",
    "measures": "This species occurs in protected areas.",
    "use_trade": null,
    "rationale": "Listed as Least Concern in view of its wide distribution, presumed large population, and because it is unlikely to be declining within its native range at nearly the rate required to qualify for listing in a threatened category.",
    "trend_justification": null,
    "taxonomic_notes": null
  },
